### MEDUSA API — Organizations, Teams & Memberships
### Install the VS Code REST Client extension to send these requests.
### Start the API and apply migrations first:
### docker compose up --build -d
### docker compose exec api alembic upgrade head
###
### Use a local development account. Public registration creates a participant.
### Organization creation requires an organizer/admin token.
### Never put real production credentials in this file.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000/api/v1
@organizerEmail = organizer@example.com
@memberEmail = member@example.com
@password = Replace-With-A-Long-Local-Test-Password
@organizationSlug = uok-rest-client
@organizationName = University of Kelaniya REST Client Test
@teamName = MEDUSA REST Client Team

### 1. Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/live

### 2. Database readiness
GET {{baseUrl}}/ready

### 3. Register organizer test account (new account only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{organizerEmail}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 4. Login as organizer
### IMPORTANT: the account must already have organizer/admin role in the database.
### If this is a newly registered participant, this request succeeds but organization creation returns 403.
# @name organizerLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username={{organizerEmail}}&password={{password}}

### 5. Create organization (organizer/admin only)
# @name createOrganization
POST {{baseUrl}}/organizations
Authorization: Bearer {{organizerLogin.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "{{organizationName}}",
  "slug": "{{organizationSlug}}",
  "description": "Local REST Client test organization"
}

### 6. List active organizations
GET {{baseUrl}}/organizations

### 7. Get organization by ID
### Set organizationId to the ID returned by request 5.
@organizationId = 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/organizations/{{organizationId}}

### 8. List teams in organization
GET {{baseUrl}}/organizations/{{organizationId}}/teams

### 9. Create a team (authenticated user becomes captain)
# @name createTeam
POST {{baseUrl}}/organizations/{{organizationId}}/teams
Authorization: Bearer {{organizerLogin.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "{{teamName}}"
}

### 10. Get team details and members
### Set teamId to the ID returned by request 9.
@teamId = 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{teamId}}

### 11. Register member test account (new account only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{memberEmail}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 12. Login as member
# @name memberLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username={{memberEmail}}&password={{password}}

### 13. Join team as member
POST {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{teamId}}/join
Authorization: Bearer {{memberLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### 14. Try joining the same team again (expected 409 Conflict)
POST {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{teamId}}/join
Authorization: Bearer {{memberLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### 15. Leave team as member (expected 204 No Content)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{teamId}}/leave
Authorization: Bearer {{memberLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### 16. Try creating an organization as a participant (expected 403 Forbidden)
POST {{baseUrl}}/organizations
Authorization: Bearer {{memberLogin.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Should Be Forbidden",
  "slug": "should-be-forbidden"
}

### 17. Duplicate organization slug (expected 409 Conflict)
### Run after request 5 succeeds.
POST {{baseUrl}}/organizations
Authorization: Bearer {{organizerLogin.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Duplicate Slug Test",
  "slug": "{{organizationSlug}}"
}

### 18. Duplicate team name in the same organization (expected 409 Conflict)
### Run after request 9 succeeds. This request uses the organizer token.
POST {{baseUrl}}/organizations/{{organizationId}}/teams
Authorization: Bearer {{organizerLogin.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "{{teamName}}"
}

### 19. Captain cannot leave before captaincy transfer is implemented (expected 409 Conflict)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/teams/{{teamId}}/leave
Authorization: Bearer {{organizerLogin.response.body.access_token}}
